        "mission_intent": "Subject: Authorization Boundary Documentation for Financial Reporting Systems \u2014 Full Specification Needed\n\nTeam, we need a comprehensive specification document that maps out the authorization boundaries for all information systems supporting our financial reporting environment, consistent with the risk management framework guidance in NIST SP 800-37 Rev. 2. For each system, the document should clearly delineate the boundary as determined by the authorizing official with input from the respective system owner, factoring in mission responsibility, management oversight, and budgetary accountability. Pay particular attention to interconnections where lower-impact systems feed data into higher-impact financial reporting platforms, and flag any cases where external service providers operate or maintain components within a boundary. Each boundary entry must include the system's security categorization, the organized set of information resources (system elements) that comprise it, the supported business processes and mission functions, and accountability assignments per Appendix F guidance. We also need to capture how each system element is implemented to satisfy organizational requirements. Please coordinate with our authorizing officials and system owners to validate all boundary determinations, and have the draft specification ready for review by the close of next quarter so we can incorporate findings into our annual financial audit risk assessment cycle.",
